 "response": "Sukukre's budget is now **$1,287K**. That comes from replaying every Finance Office update in order, starting from the $2,130K set in #0001. Messages from other teams are ignored.\n\n**How withdrawals were handled.** Each withdrawal chain was resolved from its last link backwards. A withdrawal that is not itself withdrawn cancels its target. If that target was a withdrawal, the update it had cancelled comes back into effect.\n\n| Chain | Result |\n|---|---|\n| #1138 \u2192 #0939 \u2192 #0128 \u2192 #0026 \u2192 #0011 \u2192 #0008 | #0008 stays withdrawn |\n| #0447 \u2192 #0254 \u2192 #0208 \u2192 #0139 \u2192 #0073 \u2192 #0045 | #0045 stays withdrawn |\n| #1405 \u2192 #0933 \u2192 #0204 \u2192 #0072 \u2192 #0061 | #0061 comes back (\u2212$578K) |\n| #1088 \u2192 #1050 \u2192 #0813 \u2192 #0787 \u2192 #0540 \u2192 #0359 \u2192 #0317 \u2192 #0298 | #0298 stays withdrawn |\n| #1547 \u2192 #1423 \u2192 #1302 | #1302 comes back (\u2212$514K) |\n| #1384 \u2192 #1236 \u2192 #1217 | #1217 comes back (+$554K) |\n\n**Running total.** Along the way the budget fell as low as $747K after #0642 and recovered above $3,000K after #1217. It then declined through the later updates to $1,217K after #1594. The final update, #1598 (+$70K), brings it to $1,287K.\n\nThis is a long hand calculation, so a small slip is possible. The withdrawals of #0275 (by #1430) and #0321 (by #0685) were caught during the replay rather than in the first pass.\n\nANSWER: $1287K",
